From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:33:13 -0500
Subject: fix: a passkey check pending at shutdown no longer outlives its
 profile

On Windows the passwords page asks whether the system holds passkeys. When
that has not been cached, Chromium's CredentialPresenceCacher waits for
webauthn.dll's list in a reply bound to the check. It keeps the profile as a
raw pointer and removes itself as the profile's observer when destroyed, and
it is told when the profile goes away, but it never registered as an
observer. A check still pending when the profile was destroyed kept a
dangling pointer: at shutdown the reply was destroyed after the profile and
RemoveObserver() read freed memory (an access violation in
FindWordsTest.ArcsWordsFindASpacesSession, about one run in three), and a
reply that ran after a profile was deleted wrote to that profile's prefs. It
now registers in its constructor. The next milestone has the same code.

Why: BACKLOG S-472, found while moving the pin to M157's newest point
release; the same crash was seen once on the pin before it.
Removable when: upstream registers the observer.
---
 .../webauthn/local_credential_management_win.cc      | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/webauthn/local_credential_management_win.cc b/chrome/browser/webauthn/local_credential_management_win.cc
index 150ed1f9ecb5c..56abd569d045b 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/webauthn/local_credential_management_win.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/webauthn/local_credential_management_win.cc
@@ -54,7 +54,17 @@ class CredentialPresenceCacher : public ProfileObserver {
       base::OnceCallback<void(
           std::optional<std::vector<device::DiscoverableCredentialMetadata>>)>
           callback)
-      : profile_(profile), callback_(std::move(callback)) {}
+      : profile_(profile), callback_(std::move(callback)) {
+    // Stedding (BACKLOG S-472): the destructor and OnProfileWillBeDestroyed()
+    // expect this observer to be registered, and it never was. A check still
+    // pending when the profile went away kept a dangling `profile_`: at
+    // shutdown the pending reply was destroyed after the profile and
+    // RemoveObserver() read freed memory, and a reply that ran wrote to the
+    // freed profile's prefs.
+    if (profile_) {
+      profile_->AddObserver(this);
+    }
+  }
 
   ~CredentialPresenceCacher() override {
     if (profile_) {
